/// Datasheet for `ui` — the pure LAYOUT vocabulary shared by the ui element family (panel / textedit /
/// textview / button). A "vocabulary device" like `vec`: no storage, no `gfx` — just constants + branch-free
/// helpers a DRIVER uses to stack elements inside a panel. Each element device reads its computed screen rect
/// from driver-owned columns; this module computes those rects. The dom backends scale the same render-px
/// metrics by `innerHeight/renderH` to CSS px, so native and browser lay out identically.

/// Layout metrics, render px (the panel is authored at native/render scale; the DOM scales them per viewport).
PAD     :: 18;   // frame inner padding (gap between the frame edge and its content)
GAP     :: 14;   // vertical gap between stacked elements
TITLE_H :: 34;   // title-bar height
